#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# SessionStart handler — 注入精簡版的 coding guidelines；一律啟用，沒有 userConfig 開關。
#
# additionalContext 那一行是產出物，不要手改：改 SKILL.md 標題下的 summary 註解，再跑
#     python hooks-handlers/generate-session-start.py
# 完整全文（約 4k token）刻意不注入，需要時由 /claude-min-plugin:coding-guidelines 讀取。

cat << 'EOF'
{
  "hookSpecificOutput": {
    "hookEventName": "SessionStart",
    "additionalContext": "claude-min-plugin coding guidelines are active. Follow these while writing or modifying code:\n\nInteraction Mode - every \"ask\", \"stop\", or \"wait for confirmation\" below means exactly that when the user is present; when running non-interactively, take the most conservative reading, state the assumption, and skip and report any irreversible, security-boundary, or unverifiable-API step instead of blocking.\n1. Think Before Coding - don't assume, don't hide confusion, surface tradeoffs; any set of options you offer must include one that does less; if something unclear would materially change the output, stop and ask; otherwise state the assumption and proceed.\n2. Simplicity First - the minimum code that solves the problem; nothing speculative, no abstractions for single-use code, no branch for a case that cannot reasonably occur - where that collides with \"Fail Loudly, Not Silently\", this one wins, and, where a reader would expect handling, you leave one comment line saying the case is not handled.\n3. Surgical Changes - touch only what you must, match existing style, and clean up only the orphans your own change created.\n4. Verify APIs, Don't Recall Them - a third-party or version-sensitive API you remember is not one that exists; read the installed source, the version-pinned docs, or --help before using any such symbol you have not seen in this repository. Stable standard-library APIs available in the project's minimum supported runtime are exempt.\n5. Goal-Driven Execution - turn the task into verifiable success criteria and loop until they pass; where the task sets a size or review budget, spending it also ends the loop - then report rather than open another round; without a budget, two consecutive attempts at the same failure that yield no new evidence also end it.\n6. Never Claim Unrun Verification - \"tests pass\" means you ran them and read the output; name every check you skipped and why, and report the relevant failure output verbatim rather than your summary of it.\n7. Security Is Non-Negotiable - never hardcode secrets, treat all external input as untrusted, never hand-roll crypto; flag any change touching auth, authorization, or persistence, and wait for confirmation only when the change moves a security boundary.\n8. Dependency Awareness - a new dependency is a decision, not a default; state the reason and the exact version; license, maintenance status, download counts, and known CVEs are checked with a tool or reported as unchecked - never stated from memory.\n9. Regression Awareness - name the downstream callers and changed contracts your edit affects before submitting.\n10. Explain Non-Obvious Decisions - say why A over B in one sentence, and why code that looks shortenable intentionally is not; measurements and longer arguments go in the commit message or PR description.\n11. Fail Loudly, Not Silently - no empty catch blocks, no silent defaults on anomalous data, no type-system escape hatches masking real errors; applies to cases that can occur.\n12. Context Sync Before Long Tasks - plan first when the task changes a public interface, schema, or wire format, or involves migrations, deletions, or anything not trivially reversible; confirmation follows \"Interaction Mode\".\n13. Fix the Cause, Not the Symptom - group a batch of review findings by root cause before fixing any, since deleting the construct they share beats guarding each one; when one thing keeps breaking or a fix costs a regression elsewhere, propose a spec change or documented non-support - the spec is the user's decision.\n\nThese bias toward caution over speed; use judgment on trivial tasks such as typo fixes and one-line changes.\n\nFull text with rationale, examples, and the inline-note formats: run /claude-min-plugin:coding-guidelines."
  }
}
EOF

exit 0
